   "unmapped": [
    "Rewards follow a GLM with exogenous dispersion g(tau_t) chosen adaptively by the adversary after the action and revealed after the round",
    "Generalized self-concordance |mu''| <= R_s mu'; the learner knows R_s (used in eta and lambda)",
    "Corruption c_t chosen after observing the clean reward; only the corrupted reward is observed"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "At each $t\\in[T]$, the learner receives a potentially adversarial, time-varying contextual arm-set $\\gX_t\\subset\\sR^d$ and selects an action $\\vx_t\\in\\gX_t$. After observing $\\vx_t$, the adversary selects a dispersion parameter $\\tau_t$, and a stochastic reward is then sampled as $r_t\\sim GLM(\\cdot\\mid\\vx_t,\\tau_t;\\vtheta_\\star)$. After observing $r_t$, the adversary chooses a corruption $c_t\\in\\sR$. ... The corruption budget $C$ satisfies $\\sum_{t=1}^T|c_t|\\leq C$ almost surely"
  },
